BODY_BEGIN
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000001 "use 5.006; use strict; use warnings;"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000002 "use Carp ();"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000003 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000004 "package Config::INI::Tiny;"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000005 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000006 "our $VERSION = '0.106';"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000007 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000008 "sub new { my $class = shift; bless { section0 => '', line0 => 0, pairs => 0, @_ }, $class }"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000009 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000010 "my $str = '[^\\r\\n]* [^\\r\\n\\t ]';"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000011 "my $ws  = '[\\t ]*';"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000012 "my $cmt = '[#;]'; # separate var because cf. \"Starting in Perl 5.001\" in L<perl5200delta/'Regular Expressions'>"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000013 "my $rx  = qr{\\G $ws (?: $cmt (?:$str)? | \\[ $ws ($str) $ws \\] | ([^=\\r\\n]+?) $ws = $ws ($str|) | ($str) )? $ws (?:\\z|\\n|\\r\\n?) }x;"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000014 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000015 "sub parse {"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000016 "\tmy $self = shift;"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000017 "\tmy $n = $self->{'line0'}, my @out = my $s = [ $self->{'section0'} ], pos( $_[0] ) = 0;"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000018 "\tBEGIN { utf8->import if eval { require utf8 } } # 5.6 compat"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000019 "\twhile ( ++$n, $_[0] =~ /$rx/g ) {"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000020 "\t\t; defined $2 ? push @$s, $self->{'pairs'} ? [ \"$2\", \"$3\" ] : ( \"$2\", \"$3\" )"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000021 "\t\t: defined $1 ? push @out, $s = [ \"$1\" ]"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000022 "\t\t: defined $4 ? Carp::croak map { s/\"/\\\\\"/g; qq'Bad INI syntax at line $n: \"$_\"' } \"$4\""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000023 "\t\t: ()"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000024 "\t}"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000025 "\twantarray ? @out : $out[0];"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000026 "}"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000027 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000028 "sub to_hash {"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000029 "\tmy $self = shift;"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000030 "\tmy ( @section, %config ) = do { local $self->{'pairs'}; $self->parse( $_[0] ) };"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000031 "\tshift @section unless @{ $section[0] } > 1;      # remove initial unnamed section if empty"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000032 "\tpush @{ $config{ shift @$_ } }, $_ for @section; # collect sections in HoAoA, to minimise (re)alloc work"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000033 "\t$_ = { map @$_, @$_ } for values %config;        # flatten HoAoA to HoH as cheaply as possible"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000034 "\t\\%config;"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000035 "}"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000036 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000037 "__END__"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000038 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000039 "=pod"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000040 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000041 "=encoding UTF-8"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000042 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000043 "=head1 NAME"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000044 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000045 "Config::INI::Tiny - Parse INI configuration in extremely little code"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000046 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000047 "=head1 SYNOPSIS"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000048 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000049 "=head2 Code"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000050 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000051 " use Config::INI::Tiny;"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000052 " use File::Slurper 'read_text';"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000053 " my $config = Config::INI::Tiny->new->to_hash( read_text 'myapp.ini' );"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000054 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000055 "=head2 Configuration"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000056 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000057 " global = setting"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000058 " "
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000059 " [section]"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000060 " name = value"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000061 " more = stuff"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000062 " "
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000063 " [empty section]"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000064 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000065 "=head1 DESCRIPTION"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000066 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000067 "This is an extremely small amount of code for parsing the INI configuration"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000068 "format, in its simplest form, as known from Microsoft Windows."
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000069 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000070 "Its design focuses on making it easy to extract whichever level of semantics"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000071 "you need from your configuration: whether you want to care about the order of"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000072 "properties; their recurrence; the order of sections; treating each section"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000073 "header as a separate unit; or however else you want to be able to interpret"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000074 "your configuration files E<mdash> you can."
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000075 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000076 "=head1 METHODS"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000077 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000078 "=head2 C<new>"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000079 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000080 "Instantiates an INI parser with the specified configuration."
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000081 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000082 "The parsed form consists of a list of sections as they appeared in the configuration,"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000083 "each represented by an array."
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000084 "The first element of each array is the name of the section."
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000085 "It is followed by any number of property/value pairs as they appeared in the configuration."
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000086 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000087 "This format can be modified with the following options:"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000088 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000089 "=head3 C<section0>"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000090 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000091 "The section name for properties found before the first section in the configuration."
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000092 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000093 "Defaults to the empty string, which cannot be expressed by valid configuration syntax."
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000094 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000095 "For L<Config::Tiny> compatibility, set this to an underscore (C<_>)."
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000096 "Note that a section with this name is valid syntax and can appear in a configuration."
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000097 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000098 "=head3 C<pairs>"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000099 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000100 "When true, each property/value pair within the section array is returned as"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000101 "a two-element sub-array."
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000102 "Otherwise all the pairs are returned as a single flat list."
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000103 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000104 "Defaults to false."
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000105 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000106 "=head2 C<to_hash>"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000107 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000108 "Takes a configuration in INI format as a string and returns it as a hash of"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000109 "hashes or throws an exception on syntax error."
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000110 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000111 "=head2 C<parse>"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000112 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000113 "Takes a configuration in INI format as a string and returns it in parsed form"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000114 "or throws an exception on syntax error."
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000115 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000116 "=head1 SYNTAX"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000117 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000118 "=over 3"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000119 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000120 "=item * Leading and trailing whitespace is ignored on every line."
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000121 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000122 "=item * Empty lines are ignored."
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000123 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000124 "=item * Lines that start with C<#> or C<;> are ignored."
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000125 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000126 " ; this is a comment"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000127 " # so is this"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000128 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000129 "=item * Lines enclosed in paired square brackets with any non-whitespace in between are section lines."
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000130 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000131 " [section name]"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000132 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000133 "=item * Leading and trailing whitespace in section names is ignored."
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000134 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000135 " ; these are all the same section:"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000136 " [ section name ]"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000137 " [section name  ]"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000138 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000139 "=item * Lines that contain a C<=> are property lines."
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000140 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000141 " prop name=prop value"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000142 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000143 "Everything left of the leftmost C<=> is the name of the property."
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000144 "Everything to the right of that C<=> is the value of the property."
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000145 "The name of the property cannot be empty, but the value can."
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000146 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000147 "=item * Leading and trailing whitespace in property names and values is ignored."
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000148 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000149 " ; these all have identical effect:"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000150 " prop name=prop value"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000151 " prop name  =  prop value"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000152 " prop name=    prop value"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000153 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000154 "=item * Everything else is a syntax error."
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000155 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000156 "=back"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000157 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000158 "=head1 COOKBOOK"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000159 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000160 "=head2 Emulating L<Config::Tiny::Ordered>"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000161 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000162 " my $config;"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000163 " for my $s_kv ( Config::INI::Tiny->new( section0 => '_', pairs => 1 )->parse( $content ) ) {"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000164 "     my $section_name = shift @$s_kv;"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000165 "     push @{ $config->{ $section_name } }, map +{ key => $_->[0], value => $_->[1] }, @$s_kv;"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000166 " };"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000167 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000168 "The resulting data structure is a hash of arrays instead of the hash of hashes"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000169 "that L<Config::Tiny> would produce."
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000170 "The arrays contain key/value pairs in order of their appearance in the input,"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000171 "where each pair is represented by a hash with two keys named C<key> and C<value>."
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000172 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000173 "=head2 Multi-value (and order-preserving) properties"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000174 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000175 " use Hash::MultiValue;"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000176 " "
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000177 " my $config;"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000178 " for my $s_kv ( Config::INI::Tiny->new->parse( $content ) ) {"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000179 "     my $section_name = shift @$s_kv;"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000180 "     my $section = $config->{ $section_name } ||= Hash::MultiValue->new;"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000181 "     $section->merge_flat( @$s_kv );"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000182 " }"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000183 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000184 "Consider the following configuration:"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000185 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000186 " [eth0]"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000187 " ip = 192.168.0.17"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000188 " ip = 10.0.1.253"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000189 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000190 "When using L</to_hash>, this would simply store C<10.0.1.253> as the IP for"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000191 "C<eth0>, with the C<192.168.0.17> value irretrievably lost. L<Hash::MultiValue>"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000192 "defaults to the same behaviour, but optionally allows you to still retrieve all"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000193 "other values:"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000194 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000195 " say for $config->{'eth0'}->get_all('ip');"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000196 " # 192.168.0.17"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000197 " # 10.0.1.253"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000198 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000199 "=head2 Flexibly nestable sections and properties"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000200 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000201 " sub hash_path_ref (\\%;@) {"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000202 "     my $hash = shift;"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000203 "     $hash = $hash->{ $_ } ||= {} for @_[ -@_ .. -2 ];"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000204 "     \\$hash->{ $_[-1] };"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000205 " }"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000206 " "
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000207 " my $config = {};"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000208 " for my $s_kv ( Config::INI::Tiny->new( pairs => 1 )->parse( $content ) ) {"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000209 "     my $section_name = shift @$s_kv;"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000210 "     my $section = ${ hash_path_ref %$config, split ' ', $section_name } ||= {};"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000211 "     ${ hash_path_ref %$section, split ' ', $_->[0] } = $_->[1] for @$s_kv;"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000212 " }"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000213 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000214 "This interprets spaces in section and property names as path separators,"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000215 "allowing a value like C<< $config->{'de'}{'error'}{'syntax'} >> to be specified"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000216 "in any one of the following ways, interchangeably:"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000217 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000218 " de error syntax = Syntax-Fehler"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000219 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000220 " [de]"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000221 " error syntax = Syntax-Fehler"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000222 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000223 " [de error]"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000224 " syntax = Syntax-Fehler"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000225 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000226 "The first two choices are convenient for sections with very few properties,"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000227 "to avoid having to write a section header line just for one or two properties."
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000228 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000229 "The last one is especially convenient when a section with many properties has"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000230 "a deeply nested path,"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000231 "to avoid having to repeat (part of) the path for each and every property."
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000232 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000233 "I<Caveat lector:> this creates the possibility of inconsistent configurations"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000234 "like the following:"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000235 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000236 " [foo]"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000237 " bar = 1"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000238 " "
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000239 " [foo bar]"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000240 " baz = 1"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000241 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000242 "With the given code, a configuration like this will trigger a ref stricture"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000243 "exception while parsing, because it is essentially equivalent to the following"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000244 "code:"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000245 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000246 " use strict 'refs';"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000247 " $config->{'foo'}{'bar'} = 1;"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000248 " $config->{'foo'}{'bar'}{'baz'} = 1; # boom"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000249 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000250 "Depending on use case, the ref stricture exception may or may not be sufficient"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000251 "(syntax) error handling."
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000252 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000253 "=head1 SEE ALSO"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000254 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000255 "=over 4"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000256 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000257 "=item L<Config::Tiny>"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000258 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000259 "The original basis for this module. Its design is focused on making the"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000260 "simplest operations as easy as possible, so it returns the configuration"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000261 "as a blessed hash on which you can call a method to write it back to a file."
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000262 "It does not preserve any information about the order or recurrence of either"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000263 "sections or properties."
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000264 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000265 "=item L<Config::Tiny::Ordered>"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000266 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000267 "This is a clone of L<Config::Tiny> with a more complex data structure, allowing"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000268 "it to preserve the order and recurrence of properties within sections. Section"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000269 "order and recurrence is still discarded. There is no other change in trade-offs."
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000270 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000271 "The shape of its output data structure is easy to replicate with this module,"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000272 "as shown L<in the cookbook|/Emulating Config::Tiny::Ordered>."
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000273 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000274 "=item L<Config::INI>"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000275 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000276 "An attempt at making L<Config::Tiny> flexible by breaking out the steps in the"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000277 "parser as methods, which allows parsing a different syntax. Tweaking is done by"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000278 "subclassing, which is cumbersome. If you wish to avoid reimplementing large parts"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000279 "of the module in your subclass, you are constrained by the existing call graph,"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000280 "so you must stay fairly close to both the original format and the default data"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000281 "structure shape. In other words, you can parse any format into any output, so"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000282 "long as it is I<basically> INI parsed into the default output format; or you"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000283 "can write basically your own parser."
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000284 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000285 "By contrast, Config::INI::Tiny offers no way of redefining the core INI syntax"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000286 "but instead provides an easy-to-process full-fidelity representation of its"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000287 "semantics, so that you can implement additional semantics on top of it,"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000288 "as shown L<in the cookbook|/Flexibly nestable sections and properties>."
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000289 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000290 "=back"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000291 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000292 "=head1 AUTHOR"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000293 ""
